; Stage 15 W4a / findings §3.2: `defconst` with a type annotation registered
; nothing, so every use failed with no diagnostic at the definition. W4b
; (design/stage15-stress-test/diagnostics.md §W4b) decided to REJECT the
; annotation at the `defconst` line itself, rather than accept it as a type —
; pinned by run_reject_at below. (Originally left loose here, asserting only
; "no :0:", so W4b could tighten it once the decision was made.)
(defconst K:i32 2)

(defn main ():i32
  (return K))
